I want to build an android app that is a general Nervos Network Companion App. App should have a persistent 5 button bottom menu with icons for Home, News, applications, tools,settings. Home Should be dashboard Showing chain data, price summary, the latest news item, a logo.  News should be an auto pooled list of selected Nervos Talk forum posts, Twitter Posts from selected accounts, any other links flagged by me via github integration. Applications should be links to ecosystem applications. Each link should be a encased in a full width 800x320 horizonttal panel with background artwork, Title, breif description and social media links as clickable buttons underneath the panel. Tools Should lead to a menu with network tools built into the app, for example embed daoview.org into a page. There should also be an integrated ckb console terminal off a tool button click. a terminal page in bitcoin core "console" fashion but newer and more intuitive, Settings should allow a user definable node field which defaults to a public rpc but also lists alternatives like ankr, utxo global. Lets formulate a plan for agentic development 

Here’s a solid agentic development plan.

## Recommended stack

**Android app:** Kotlin + Jetpack Compose
**Storage:** Room DB + DataStore
**Networking:** Ktor or Retrofit
**Background polling:** WorkManager
**Web embeds:** Android WebView
**Charts:** Compose chart library or custom Canvas
**Terminal console:** custom Compose UI calling JSON-RPC against selected CKB node

CKB has official JSON-RPC docs, and Ankr/GetBlock-style hosted node providers exist, so the app should treat RPC providers as configurable rather than hardcoded. ([Nervos CKB][1])

